ith identical content. Editor content intact (2 experience entries) and selected template still Modern.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Card menu > Duplicate created \\\"QA Automation Resume (Copy)\\\" carrying all source content. Renamed the copy via the rename dialog to \\\"Senior SDET Application\\\". Edited the copy (name \\\"Alice COPY Tester\\\", email copy@example.com, new summary); reopening the source showed it unchanged (Alice M. Tester / alice@example.com / original summary).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dashboard holds 6 distinct resumes: Zebra Consulting Variation (Zed Consultant), Senior SDET Application (duplicate, independently edited), QA Automation Resume, plus 3 seeded ones. Each opens with its own content, template and title; create/duplicate/rename/delete controls all available per card.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"rEsUmE\\\" (mixed case) matched the 4 titles containing \\\"resume\\\" case-insensitively, excluding \\\"Senior SDET Application\\\" and \\\"Zebra Consulting Variation\\\". Sort \\\"Oldest First\\\" ordered Jan 20 2024 -> Feb 10 2024 -> Feb 25 2024 -> Aug 27 2026; \\\"Newest First\\\" reversed it. Clearing the search restored all 6 resumes.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No creation-date filter feature exists\", \"actual\": \"The dashboard exposes only three controls: \\\"New Resume\\\", a text search box (\\\"Search resumes...\\\"), and a sort dropdown (Newest/Oldest/Title A-Z/Title Z-A). An exhaustive scan of all input/select/button elements found zero date or date-range inputs (0 elements of type=date or type=month) and no exact-date or from/to filter UI, therefore no date criterion to clear either. The text search does not act as a date filter: entering \\\"Feb 25, 2024\\\" returned 0 results (\\\"No resumes found - Try a different search term\\\") even though a resume carries that date.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No validation of invalid date periods\", \"actual\": \"In an experience entry, setting End Date 2019-05 with Start Date 2020-01 (end before start) was accepted with no error message or toast. Setting Start Date to a future month 2030-03 (today 2026-08-27) was also accepted silently. The month inputs have no min/max attributes and no inline feedback appears in the entry panel.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Experience & education dates are input type=\\\"month\\\"; preview renders \\\"Jan 2020 - Jun 2022\\\", \\\"Jul 2022 - Dec 2024\\\", \\\"Sep 2015 - Jun 2019\\\". Checking \\\"I currently work here\\\" cleared end-date value to \\\"\\\" and set disabled=true; preview showed \\\"Jan 2020 - Present\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence — all created, edited, duplicated, renamed and deleted resume versions are lost on reload\", \"actual\": \"Before reload the dashboard held 5 resumes: \\\"Senior SDET Application\\\" (duplicated + renamed), \\\"QA Automation Resume\\\" (created + heavily edited + renamed), and the 3 seeded ones, with \\\"Zebra Consulting Variation\\\" successfully deleted. localStorage and sessionStorage were both completely empty (0 keys). After reloading http://localhost:7005/ the dashboard reset to only the 3 original seeded resumes (Product Designer, Marketing Manager, Software Engineer). The created/edited/duplicated/renamed resumes vanished and the deleted one was not persisted as deleted — state is in-memory only.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Dashboard rename dialog accepts a whitespace-only title, leaving the resume with an empty title; no validation feedback anywhere\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard card menu > Rename on \\\"QA Automation Resume (Copy)\\\": entered \\\"   \\\" (three spaces) and clicked Save. The dialog closed and the rename was ACCEPTED — the card title is now empty (dashboard.resumes.item.5b8lzf8w56l has name \\\"\\\" and renders no heading text). No validation message or toast appeared. Separately, the in-editor title rename does reject empty/whitespace input and keeps the previous title, but it also gives no validation feedback of any kind.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing \\\"Alice M. Tester\\\" into contact.full-name immediately updated preview.contact.name to the same value with no save/refresh. Earlier, template switches (Modern/Classic/Minimal) re-rendered the preview instantly, and summary/experience/education/skills edits appeared in preview text immediately.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Moving Education above Experience and toggling Skills visibility updated the preview immediately (Education rendered before Work Experience; Skills disappeared then reappeared). After navigating tabs, going back to the dashboard and reopening the resume, the custom order (contact, summary, education, experience, skills) and visibility states were preserved and still reflected in the preview.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edits made across Contact/Summary/Experience/Education/Skills/Template/Sections tabs were retained without any explicit save when moving between tabs, navigating back to the dashboard and reopening the resume. Dashboard card showed \\\"Updated Aug 27, 2026\\\" (today) and template \\\"Modern\\\", reflecting the update.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Modern style with long content (910px document): preview renders every visible section with content (contact, About Me summary, Academics education, Career History with both entries and full descriptions, Core Strengths skills). Preview container has no clipped overflow (scrollHeight==clientHeight); page scrolls (body 1130px vs 720px viewport) and after scrolling to bottom the last section \\\"Core Strengths / Playwright\\\" is fully within the viewport (top 277, bottom 361).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After switching editor tabs, returning to dashboard and reopening \\\"QA Automation Resume\\\": contact fields all retained (Alice M. Tester / alice@example.com / 555-0100 / Berlin, DE / linkedin.com/in/alice / alice.dev), summary, both experience entries with full descriptions and dates, education (TU Berlin, BSc Computer Science, GPA 3.9, Sep 2015 - Jun 2019) and the Playwright skill all present in the preview.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Copy->original: editing the copy (full-name, email, summary) left the original at \\\"Alice M. Tester\\\"/\\\"alice@example.com\\\"/original summary, with no \\\"COPY\\\" text in its preview. Original->copy: setting the original's phone to \\\"555-ORIGINAL\\\" left the copy's phone at \\\"555-0100\\\" with its own edited name/email/summary intact.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Renamed \\\"Untitled Resume\\\" to \\\"QA Automation Resume\\\"; editor.title reads \\\"QA Automation Resume\\\" and the dashboard card (key ldxp7yi7o4) shows the same title.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Customized Summary heading not rendered in the Minimal style\", \"actual\": \"Section headings were customized to \\\"About Me\\\" (summary), \\\"Career History\\\", \\\"Academics\\\", \\\"Core Strengths\\\". Modern preview shows all four; Classic shows all four uppercased (ABOUT ME / ACADEMICS / CAREER HISTORY / CORE STRENGTHS). Minimal renders ACADEMICS, CAREER HISTORY and CORE STRENGTHS but the summary section (visible and containing text) is rendered with no heading at all — preview text goes straight from the contact block to the summary body, and preview headings are only H1 name, ACADEMICS, CAREER HISTORY, CORE STRENGTHS. \\\"About Me\\\"/\\\"ABOUT ME\\\" is absent from the Minimal preview.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
      }
    ]
  }
