    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 21 checklist items have been tested and recorded.\n\n**Results: 16 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core resume-building experience is solid — creation, editing across all content areas, template switching, section reordering/visibility, live preview, duplication with proper data isolation, and title/date sorting with case-insensitive search all work correctly.\n\n**Five defects found:**\n\n1. **CS-11 (most severe)** — No persistence layer at all. `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` are completely empty; reloading resets the app to its 3 seeded resumes, discarding every created, edited, duplicated, renamed, and deleted version.\n\n2. **FT-19** — The creation-date filter feature is entirely absent. The dashboard has only text search and a sort dropdown; there are zero date inputs, so exact-date and date-range narrowing don't exist.\n\n3. **CS-21** — The dashboard rename dialog *accepts* a whitespace-only title, leaving a resume with a blank, unlabeled card. (The in-editor rename correctly rejects it, but silently — neither path gives validation feedback.)\n\n4. **CS-9** — No date-period validation whatsoever. An end date preceding the start date and a future start date were both accepted silently, with no min/max constraints on the month inputs.\n\n5. **CT-20** — The Minimal template omits the customizable Summary heading entirely; the summary body renders with no heading, while Modern and Classic both display it correctly.\n\nNotably, CS-21 and CS-9 share a root cause worth flagging to the team: validation rules appear to be specified but not implemented — invalid input is either silently discarded or silently accepted, leaving users with no feedback in both cases."
  }
}
